        {
          "id": "the_three_pollutant_processes_and_the_chain_between_them",
          "description": "The run's whole pollutant scope, unpacked from `runspecpollutantprocess` and `runspecchainedto` rather than written down. 9101 is Total Energy x Running Exhaust and is the only ENERGY pollutant here, so it is the only one S18 divides by 1,055,055.9; 11710 is PM2.5 Tirewear x Tirewear and carries its own emissionrate rows; 10710 is PM10 Tirewear, which carries NONE and is chained from 11710. The chain is one edge of the model's edge list: output 10710, input 11710. The other two pollutant-processes appear on no edge, so their chain term is an empty sum and vanishes without a branch.\n\nTHE PROCESS IDS ARE 1 AND 10 AND THAT MATTERS TWICE. It is the process, not the pollutant, that decides which generator wrote a pollutant-process's operating-mode weights (`rspp_usesAvgSpeedModes`), and it is the process digit that the SCC and the output's own processID column carry -- 2201210410 against brake wear's 2201210409, one digit apart.",
