        {
          "id": "the_drive_cycle_scaffolding_is_a_single_physics_row_and_two_data_thresholds",
          "description": "The three facts W's correctness rests on that are not W itself: the braking thresholds are READ from operatingmode's Braking row rather than written as drivecycle.rs's -2.0 and -1.0 literals; the drive-cycle axis is exactly the vehicles this run drives, which here is one; and every average-speed bin's bracketing weights sum to 1, which is what catches a duplicated bracket speed or a bin with no bracket.\n\nTHE MIDDLE ONE IS THREE ASSERTIONS AND NOT ONE AS OF 7d-next. It used to be `run_physicsRowsSelected == 1` per source type, and it was the document's statement that a source type has one vehicle -- which is true of a passenger car and false of everything heavier, so it read as a fact about the model and was really a fact about the fixture. Now it is the recomputation of `n_physicsRow` (1 here, 4 at source types 21 and 32, 40 at five), plus the two ways the axis can be wrong without changing the shape of anything: a selected vehicle past the end of the axis, and a rate row whose regulatory class has no vehicle at all. Both are silent and both are LOW, which is the failure mode `run_sourceBinsDropped` was added for one relation up.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "assertions": [
