        {
          "id": "the_cohort_row_set_is_the_same_125_for_both_rate_paths",
          "description": "125 of the 164 candidates survive `stmyFraction > 0`, and all 125 reach an emissionrate row, for BOTH computed pollutant-processes -- which is the claim that lets one cohort rank serve all three output blocks and is asserted rather than assumed. `pp_selectedBinCount` is 125, 0, 125: the middle zero is the chained pollutant, which has no pollutantprocessmodelyear rows and therefore no source-bin distribution of its own, and whose 125 output rows come from the chain instead -- `run_chainedRowCount` counts them. `run_binSelectionTotal` at 250 is the same fact summed, and would still be 250 if the two rate paths selected DIFFERENT 125s, which is why the per-pollutant-process counts are asserted beside it.\n\nTHE THREE COUNTS ARE OVER BINS AND `cohortSurvivorCount` IS OVER COHORTS, AND THIS RUN IS WHERE THE TWO COINCIDE. A passenger car's `samplevehiclepopulation` rows are one per (model year, fuel type) -- regulatory class 20 throughout, engine technology 1 or 30 but never both in one cohort -- so `n_sourceBin` is 1 here and the bin relation IS the cohort relation, row for row. `run_sourceBinsDropped` is what says the 1 is enough rather than merely unrefuted: it counts the bins a selected cohort holds beyond the last slot, and a light commercial truck would put 123 of them there.\n\nTHAT THE TWO RATE PATHS AGREE ON THE 125 IS NOT THE SAME CLAIM HERE AS IN process-brakewear, AND IT IS LESS OBVIOUS. There the two paths met different source bins because their shortModYrGroupIDs differed; here 11710's is 0 on every model year, so its 31 emissionrate source bins are distinguished by regulatory class, engine technology and fuel alone. A cohort that reached a 9101 rate and no 11710 rate would show up as a count below 125 rather than as a missing output row, because the output relation's rank is built once.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.cohortSurvivorCount",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 125.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.run_binSelectionTotal",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 250.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
