        {
          "id": "the_worked_examples_reach_MOVESOutput_in_all_three_blocks",
          "description": "docs/process-tirewear.md 6.1-6.5, asserted against the numbers MOVESOutput stores rather than against this document's own. Four rows per block, chosen so that every factor is exercised somewhere and the two chained blocks can be checked against each other: (MY 1980, gasoline) is the largest 9101 base rate; (MY 2020, gasoline) the largest activity; (MY 2000, electricity) is the row the EV efficiency divisor and the live EV temperature factor both act on, and it is the smallest cell in the fixture. 5.46494 / 0.819737 is 6.66670 and 0.484812 / 0.0727215 is 6.66670, so the two PM blocks check the chain against each other as well as against the reference. The SCCs are exact integers and are asserted exactly -- 2201210401 for the energy block and 2201210410 for both PM blocks, and an SCC whose process digits read 09 instead of 10 relabels tire wear as brake wear and still passes a per-pollutant sum.",
