        {
          "id": "the_air_toxics_ratio_is_two_generators_and_this_mount_can_only_see_one",
          "description": "`ATRatio` is EMPTY in the default database and MOVES writes it at run time in two halves (docs/esm-conventions.md 73). This mount is a TIRE-WEAR run, so `atbaseemissions` and `atrationongas` are copied at zero rows and no air toxic is selected -- which makes it the right place to check three things a `process-airtoxics` comparison cannot.\n\nFIRST, THE CLOSED FORM IS INDEPENDENT OF THE RUN. `atx_suppliedClosedFormRatio` reads nothing but this document's own coefficients and the county's supplied formulations, so it has a value here although nothing consumes it. The THIRTEEN numbers below face a SECOND INDEPENDENT EVALUATION of the same `generalFuelRatioExpression` strings -- Python `math` over the same substituted fuel properties -- and not the reference (docs/esm-conventions.md 35.4); they agree with the snapshot's own captured `atratio` to 1.0e-10 on benzene and 9.6e-08 on formaldehyde, and that comparison is `runspecs/process-airtoxics.esm`'s job rather than this test's. Butadiene is 0.0 because the string ends in `*(0.0)`: a ratio that IS zero, which emits a row of zeros rather than dropping one (conventions 30.1).\n\nROWS 7 TO 14 ARE THE THREE TOXICS THE AIR-TOXICS RUNG ADDED SECOND, AND THEY ARE WHERE THE FORMS RUN OUT. Row 7 is ETHANOL before model year 2001, and it is form 4 -- a STEP in the ethanol volume, `IF(E<0.1, 0, IF(E<6, 0.01195, IF(E<9, 0.01912, 0.0239)))`. This county's formulation carries 10 volume percent, so it lands in the top band at 0.0239 flat, and the three breakpoints below it are asserted by nothing here: a step function checked at ONE point checks the band it is in and not the step. Rows 12 to 14 are ACROLEIN, whose string is a bare constant, carried as form 1 with a zero slope rather than as a fifth arm -- so those three assertions are also the check that a zero slope really does make `centered_linear_ratio` return its scale. Rows 8 to 11 are ethanol and ACETALDEHYDE after model year 2000, form 3 like formaldehyde, and their E85 rows carry the two remaining `least(10, ETOHVolume)` clamps in this table.\n\nSECOND, AN EMPTY TABLE MUST GIVE ZERO AND NOT A NaN. The complex-model half divides by VOC's base emission, and with `atbaseemissions` at zero rows both sides of that quotient are 0. `atr_baseEmissions` is 0 here and `atr_suppliedComplexRatio` is 0 rather than NaN, which is F56's rule -- an arm over an empty relation contributes nothing -- reached this time through a DIVISION and not a sum.\n\nTHIRD, THE REFERENCE MODEL-YEAR GROUP IS A KEY. `cmxcfg_baseModelYearGroupID` and `cmxcfg_meanModelYearGroupID` were the literal 19502000 until the `airtoxicsA` engine arrived; the air-toxics configurations sit at group 0, their base fuel is formulation 96 and not 99, and their centring values are a different set. All three criteria configurations agree with each other, so none of them could have found this (conventions 73.1). The CENTRING itself cannot be checked here and the last assertion says so out loud: this execution copy's `meanfuelparameters` has ZERO rows, so `cmx_hasCentering` is 0 at every property of every configuration and the complex model runs uncentred -- which costs nothing on a tire-wear run and 7.4 percent on an air-toxics one, because a centre cancels in a linear term and VOC is the only configuration here whose polynomial has squared ones. That is conventions 73.2, and `runspecs/process-airtoxics.esm` is the only thing in this repository that checks it.\n\nWHAT RUNS THESE ASSERTIONS, WHICH IS NOT `run-tests.sh`. F47: a mounted component's inline tests are not discovered, and this model is only ever reached through a mount, so the suite's 952 inline assertions do NOT include this file's 153. The suite watches F47 two-sided and will go red the day that changes. Until then these twenty are checked by `esm simulate spikes/7c/tirewear_mount.esm --observed <variable>` and by reading the number, which is how every expected value here was obtained and re-obtained; they are written as assertions rather than as prose so that the day F47 is retired they start running rather than start being written.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.atx_suppliedClosedFormRatio",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.04713198020990642,
              "coords": {
                "airtoxicsform_rows": 1,
                "runspeccounty_rows": 1,
                "runspecmonth_rows": 1,
                "runspecyear_rows": 1
              }
